   "title": "The Mongols hold the spring",
   "time": "Early September 1260",
   "narrative": "Hulegu has taken most of his army back east, and Kitbuqa is left in Syria with a single tumen, Georgian and Armenian vassals, and the levies of two Ayyubid princes. Learning that the Mamluks are marching north, he gathers his scattered men and takes up a position at the spring of Ain Jalut, where Mount Gilboa shelters his flank and the stream gives water and grazing for the horses. His camp is already pitched when the Mamluk vanguard arrives.",
